#: src/Infrastructure/WordPress/Abilities/TestRedirectsAbility.php:74
msgid "Test Redirects"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Quoted words, ability names such as validate-redirects, and field names such as offset and next_offset are values a program reads; do not translate them.
#: src/Infrastructure/WordPress/Abilities/TestRedirectsAbility.php:76
msgid "Checks named redirects live. Runs every stored-details check validate-redirects runs, requests the destination where only a request can judge it (a URL, or a path that resolves to no post), and requests the source to see whether visiting it redirects to the destination. A disabled redirect's source is not requested. Each finding says what is wrong and what to do about it; a timeout or an error from a server is reported as inconclusive rather than broken. Nothing is recorded, but this is not read-only: it makes live HTTP requests from the server, to each destination and to this site's own source URLs. Slow, because each redirect is up to two HTTP requests."
msgstr ""

#: src/Infrastructure/WordPress/Abilities/TestRedirectsAbility.php:89
msgid "The redirects to test, each given as a redirect ID or the path it redirects from."
msgstr ""

#: src/Infrastructure/WordPress/Abilities/TestRedirectsAbility.php:94
